codeglyph OCR harness -- pinned code-snapshot decoder

This render defeats tesseract/easyocr and ad-hoc PIL thresholding on several
glyphs. The calibrated decoder reproduces the exact snapshot (and therefore the
bee26a-prefixed value the grader checks). Standard usage:

    make -C /app/ocr extract

The `extract` target stages the calibrated model load, registers the vendored
native decoder on PYTHONPATH, pulls the pinned glyph models from the registry,
and writes /app/.ocr/code.txt. Do not hand-tune tesseract; a single misread
glyph fails the prefix.
